ose who have already bought the book, here is the most important question of them all- can ghouls learn Devotions? Yes or no? Settle that argument once and for all!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:19:15-08:00","id":1163709,"title":"","content":"I'm most curious about the Dhampir. They're almost as high as werewolves and Mokol\u00e9 as my favorite playable supernatural character types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:21:14-08:00","id":1163710,"title":"","content":"Ugh, whoever wrote the Werewolf bit in the Dhampir section seems to have forgot that Wyrm Taint isn't a thing in CofD, based on the language used. Not impressed with how badly that syncs up with the fluff in the Werewolf books themselves about Vampires. Liking the rest of that section though (still reading through the book).<br /> <br /> And I don't see Devotions mentioned in the ghoul section at all, but that was just a quick ctrl f. I'll take a more in depth look later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 11-29-2017, 05:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:24:57-08:00","id":1163712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163707#post1163707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have already bought the book, here is the most important question of them all- can ghouls learn Devotions? Yes or no? Settle that argument once and for all!</div> </div> </div> </div>It's unclear, at least specifically. Ghouls aren't limited to the Disciplines of their Regnant and they seem to be able to learn other things, but it never mentions Devotions by name.<br /> <br /> 'Vampires may \u201cgift\u201d their ghouls augmentations, in the form of scarring tattoos to imply ownership, a crash indoctrination course to alter a ghoul into something more willingly subservient, or experimental Discipline powers to increase a servant\u2019s arsenal and see whether a ghoul is capable of using Theban Sorcery. These deviant ghouls, as other thralls know them, inevitably snap under the strain of experimentation, either descending into a vegetative state or acting with uncontrollable rage against their former companions and masters.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163710#post1163710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, whoever wrote the Werewolf bit in the Dhampir section seems to have forgot that Wyrm Taint isn't a thing in CofD, based on the language used. Not impressed with how badly that syncs up with the fluff in the Werewolf books themselves about Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it does imply that werewolves kill vampires out of hand because 'they're evil,' the werewolves that are gung-ho about killing vampires (primarily Pure) do think that.<br /> <br /> The art is vaguely Apocalyptian too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-29-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:39:25-08:00","id":1163717,"title":"","content":"Not sure how reliable <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1143328-ghoul-questions?p=1144851#post1144851\">this</a> offhand post from a couple months back should be taken to be, but... that bit about ghouls and Devotions <i>was</i> apparently supposed to make it into the book. Hrmm.<br /> I'd give a more thorough read myself and see if it's somewhere else in the book, but I can't reasonably buy it until Friday...<br /> <br /> Err, any mention of animal ghouls or mandragora?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T14:44:11-08:00","id":1163720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163717#post1163717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err, any mention of animal ghouls or mandragora?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, almost a page each, I think.<br /> <br /> A Nosferatu ghoul'd some cockroaches, unaware of how fast they reproduce, and unknowingly created a massive ghoul family of them that resisted extermination.<br /> <br /> There's also stats for small (rosebush), medium and large (black locust tree, giant pitcher plant) mandragora. And a cool picture of someone torn in half or being disposed of by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-29-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T15:01:31-08:00","id":1163727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163712#post1163712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it does imply that werewolves kill vampires out of hand because 'they're evil,' the werewolves that are gung-ho about killing vampires (primarily Pure) do think that.<br /> <br /> The art is vaguely Apocalyptian too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, it doesn't really match as a sweeping generalization with 2e's thematics so far, in my opinion. And I'm seeing more bits of that sort of thing here and there throughout it, like Werewolves are still the wyrm-hunting vamp-predators they are in WoD. I do not like it one bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, they actually used the words 'werewolf Kinfolk' in the book. Now I'm SURE the writer came from a WoD werewolf background.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 11-29-2017, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T15:03:36-08:00","id":1163728,"title":"","content":"Ooh, not just animal ghouls but animal ghoul <i>families</i>... makes me want to poke at an old NPC idea again. Also glad to hear that mandragora got some more attention; always liked them for some reason. Most of a page, while not quite the same as their treatment in 1e's <i>Ghouls</i> book, is very welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T16:01:48-08:00","id":1163742,"title":"","content":"Now that I've gotten my venom out of the way, I WILL mention I absolutely love Dhampir as a template, mechanically speaking. Twists/Themes and Malisons are very cool, and overall they feel unique and interesting without being overpowered.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":1130,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","user":"falco1029","date":". 11-29-2017, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T16:17:11-08:00","id":1163748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163712#post1163712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's unclear, at least specifically. Ghouls aren't limited to the Disciplines of their Regnant and they seem to be able to learn other things, but it never mentions Devotions by name.<br /> <br /> 'Vampires may \u201cgift\u201d their ghouls augmentations, in the form of scarring tattoos to imply ownership, a crash indoctrination course to alter a ghoul into something more willingly subservient, or experimental Discipline powers to increase a servant\u2019s arsenal and see whether a ghoul is capable of using Theban Sorcery. These deviant ghouls, as other thralls know them, inevitably snap under the strain of experimentation, either descending into a vegetative state or acting with uncontrollable rage against their former companions and masters.'<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While it does imply that werewolves kill vampires out of hand because 'they're evil,' the werewolves that are gung-ho about killing vampires (primarily Pure) do think that.<br /> <br /> The art is vaguely Apocalyptian too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hey the anniversary edition of Apocalypses corebook has a reference to a storm Lord!<br /> <br /> so sadly this kind of BS is something we must live with.<br /> <br /> same authors working on similar but distinct projects. bound to happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T16:47:57-08:00","id":1163760,"title":"","content":"What is the general power level of the dhampir, how high a level of disciplines can they learn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:11:30-08:00","id":1163767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163760#post1163760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the general power level of the dhampir, how high a level of disciplines can they learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have unique powers and don't learn disciplines at all.<br /> <br /> Overall, I'd place them above a mortal with supernatural merits or one of the Wolf-Blooded, below one of the Demon-Blooded, and roughly-equivalent to Ghouls, though they lack a lot of the raw power Ghouls can take advantage of via Disciplines and actual Vitae use, their abilities are a much more diversified toolkit that is uniquely suited to engaging with (and manipulating) both Kindred society and the broader supernatural in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 11-29-2017, 08:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:26:27-08:00","id":1163773,"title":"","content":"There are rules for ghoul families? If so, have they changed from 1st edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:33:13-08:00","id":1163777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163773#post1163773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are rules for ghoul families? If so, have they changed from 1st edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've only glanced through the section, but I'm not seeing any mechanics for their creation. There are a lot of guidelines, example families, and good explorations of the hows and whys.<br /> <br /> There are new Ghoul merits and Conditions that help facilitate families, but no strict rules for creation like there are for eg. Werewolf Packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:42:34-08:00","id":1163781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163712#post1163712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The art is vaguely Apocalyptian too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed something very jarring about the werewolf art, and I think you hit the nail on the head.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I was pretty disappointed in a large chunk of the art in this book, though a couple of the images are wonderful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-29T17:58:18-08:00","id":1163784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163707#post1163707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have already bought the book, here is the most important question of them all- can ghouls learn Devotions? Yes or no? Settle that argument once and for all!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Impernious, who I'm getting is a writer, has posted this in the errata.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1163716-half-damned-errata-thread?p=1163735#post1163735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self: Include brief sentence making it explicit that ghouls can learn devotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I'm guessing they can. I also checked a previous argument on it and they confirmed it there too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T01:46:38-08:00","id":1163847,"title":"","content":"Do Revrents get anything? Is there any upside to being one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:16:14-08:00","id":1163857,"title":"","content":"Revenants get merits and a new Discipline that's more or less unique to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:25:24-08:00","id":1163862,"title":"","content":"Oh goodie, when you say more or less do you mean that it isn't very useful to full kindred or that they can't learn it? What would happen if a Reverent learnt that Discipline and was then uplifted into a clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:27:32-08:00","id":1163863,"title":"","content":"The new Revenant tools are pretty damn cool and thematic too. The Discipline is exclusive to Rev and XP gets refunded if uplifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T04:30:00-08:00","id":1163864,"title":"","content":"Revenants now have a merit called &quot;Fertile Vitae&quot; which lets them embrace other people as revenants. There are entire communities of them that operate mostly independently of kindred.<br /> <br /> I figured that would be a thing, because otherwise the idea that revenants are sort of proto-vampires doesn't work if they can't propagate themselves.<br /> <br /> There is a sidebar talking about a &quot;lost&quot; discipline that works the same as the revenant-only one, except that kinderd can also learn it, but I'm not sure why because half the powers would be useless to full vampires because they circumvent revenant-specific problems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 11-30-2017, 07:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:05:30-08:00","id":1163871,"title":"","content":"The first dot has some extreme niche uses for a vampire, but is mostly useless. The third dot does absolutely nothing. The fourth dot is maybe useful depending on if regular vampires can feed directly from ghouls' Vitae pool. Second and fifth dot are useful, but the second dot becomes worthless as soon as the vampire is unable to feed from animals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:20:42-08:00","id":1163872,"title":"","content":"Thanks, I'm waiting for the physical but it's good to know what I'll be getting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:25:08-08:00","id":1163874,"title":"","content":"Buying the PDF grants you a coupon for the physical so the total would match the PDF+physical combo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T05:38:36-08:00","id":1163876,"title":"","content":"I've always assumed that if you totally drain a ghoul they'll instinctively spend any vitae to heal the damage and not die so you can get at it that way. <br /> <br /> But that might actually interfere with the third dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:49:42-08:00","id":1163917,"title":"","content":"If you drain things with Vitae I think you take the Vitae first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T07:57:45-08:00","id":1163921,"title":"","content":"That's the case for strix, but there's no indication that vampires follow suit.<br /> <br /> Also it's inconvenient when you want to feed from a ghoul without taking the vitae you just gave them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:02:58-08:00","id":1163923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163921#post1163921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the case for strix, but there's no indication that vampires follow suit.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from the diablerie section.<br /> <br /> P101, 'Once a Kindred victim is completely without Vitae, each point that would otherwise be taken becomes instead one point of lethal damage.'<br /> <br /> Of course since ghouls don't exactly have huge Vitae pools you could just drain them in one attack or beat them and overcome their healing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:06:23-08:00","id":1163924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163707#post1163707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For those who have already bought the book, here is the most important question of them all- can ghouls learn Devotions? Yes or no? Settle that argument once and for all!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That question was settled in a thread on here when a developer popped in and said yes that was always the intention and they would include a note in the half damned book ( I am not sure if that not was or was not actually included ) I didn't click the link,but I think Sconce referenced it in their post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:08:30-08:00","id":1163925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rickayelm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163760#post1163760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the general power level of the dhampir, how high a level of disciplines can they learn.</div> </div> </div> </div>What was said above. Dhampiri do not have Disciplines, they have the fact that the very nature of being life born from death means they all have Fate Itself as their godparent. They have Twists, somewhat conceptual control over destiny, and besides their Beast being a second Vice that only rears its head when the dhampir is stressed, they all have a third Anchor, Destiny. Which they get Willpower from pursuing or actively thwarting, with both achievement and utter denial of resulting in a full refresh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:09:57-08:00","id":1163927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163917#post1163917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you drain things with Vitae I think you take the Vitae first.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is for Strix drinking Vampires and Vampires drinking vampires, because vitae is all a vampire has and because, as someone pointed out, your ghoul would no longer be a viable food source if it happened that way on mortals. <br /> <br /> They take blood and turn it into vitae... but vampires only have vitae, so that's what they would have to take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T08:44:10-08:00","id":1163937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163927#post1163927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that it is for Strix drinking Vampires and Vampires drinking vampires, because vitae is all a vampire has and because, as someone pointed out, your ghoul would no longer be a viable food source if it happened that way on mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls aren't really meant to be food sources, they're meant to be servants. And if you're drinking from them, not only does the blood taste bleh (see: Ghouls) but even if you don't drain their Vitae, you're doing damage to them that they have reason to heal with Vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:13:54-08:00","id":1163991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163937#post1163937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls aren't really meant to be food sources, they're meant to be servants. And if you're drinking from them, not only does the blood taste bleh (see: Ghouls) but even if you don't drain their Vitae, you're doing damage to them that they have reason to heal with Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. If you think of Vitae as life-force then it just doesn't make sense. How does Bill end up with surplus life-force to fuel his supernatural powers(like not aging) if you take 1 Vitae from Bill, then give it back, but now his body needs to spend days repairing that damage from when you took it in the first place?<br /> <br /> <br /> Yes I know, Magic, but I find it easier to suspend disbelief if the magic follows some basic consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 11-30-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:14:11-08:00","id":1163992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163925#post1163925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was said above. Dhampiri do not have Disciplines, they have the fact that the very nature of being life born from death means they all have Fate Itself as their godparent. They have Twists, somewhat conceptual control over destiny, and besides their Beast being a second Vice that only rears its head when the dhampir is stressed, they all have a third Anchor, Destiny. Which they get Willpower from pursuing or actively thwarting, with both achievement and utter denial of resulting in a full refresh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me expand on this response a bit:<br /> <br /> Though it's a bit hard to piece together (the dhampir section is all over the place) they not only do not have Disciplines, they cannot learn them--because they are immune to becoming ghouls (but not immune to bonds). They also cannot be embraced. Both of these are from throw-away lines in disparate sections, challenged by other text on mindset indicating that they can aspire to become immortals like their undead parent.<br /> <br /> They &quot;like&quot; to drink blood and vitae, but apparently gain absolutely no benefit from doing so, except bonds and addiction rolls. This is... essentially a stiff middle finger toward the player, making them harder splats to roleplay, IMO. <br /> <br /> It's unclear as well whether dhampir age and die of old age normally--I believe the intent is for them to do so, but other text implies that their vampire parent gains a valuable, long-term benefit for grooming their 20-year+ investment. If they cannot be ghouled and age normally, dhampiri have as much utility as a mortal with a short stack of supernatural merits--and for some of such merits out there, rather less utility.<br /> <br /> You do get an extra route to recover willpower (destiny), which is needed since you burn willpower to activate twists. In a somewhat cool fashion you can substitute a new destiny for one you fulfill, so if you are working with your ST on this you could lay out a clear line of breadcrumbs to follow with some mechanical benefits. If you don't work with your ST? Well you're not going to get much good out of destiny.<br /> <br /> Twists, mechanically, are structured to not exceed three dots in power level. And they're pretty mild, offering more utility than crunch. You will not get any kind of benefit on par with, say, the physical disciplines, but you could certainly surprise someone!<br /> <br /> There is no healing mechanism that I see, beyond normal mortal healing. Not even a twist. This is likely to be an issue during play, since their sorcery mechanism relies on damaging themselves. On the other hand, that's more meaningful if it takes you a week to recover....<br /> <br /> My quick evaluation? I'll have to houserule a few things to use them. Namely dispensing with the no-embrace and no-ghoul restrictions, which seem unnecessary. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T11:35:54-08:00","id":1163996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163937#post1163937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls aren't really meant to be food sources, they're meant to be servants. And if you're drinking from them, not only does the blood taste bleh (see: Ghouls) but even if you don't drain their Vitae, you're doing damage to them that they have reason to heal with Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have not cranked through all of the Half Damned book so if it's in there, I apologize. I do not see anywhere in the 2E core book that ghoul blood tastes bad. Do you have a page number? Also... ghouls are meant to be servants and we all know there are about 100 different ways to <i>serve </i> someone. Food, drink, sex, cleaning, fighting, bookkeeping, laundry, driving, .... whatever. Sure you do damage to them, but that doesn't mean you CAN'T feed from them. especially in a pinch...<br /> <br /> Also there is a merit in the &quot;GHOUL and MORTAL&quot; called producer which allows your ghoul or human bloodbonded servant to produce twice as much vitae for you than the average Joe. That merit would make absolutely no sense to be in the book at all, or at very least THAT section of it, if you couldnt feed off a ghoul. Also that merit heavily heavily implies that when you do drink from a ghoul, you take their blood and leave their vitae reserve alone. <br /> <br /> <br /> Producer (\u2022)<br /> You may suffer a medical condition that means you produce<br /> a higher blood volume, or suffer from a thickening of the blood<br /> caused by too many red blood cells. Or your condition may be<br /> completely mystical and never show up under a microscope.<br /> However it manifests, you produce extra Vitae when a Kindred<br /> drinks from you.<br /> Prerequisite: Human or Ghoul<br /> Effect: For every point of lethal damage caused by feeding,<br /> Kindred gain two Vitae from your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:00:08-08:00","id":1164004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163996#post1163996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also there is a merit in the &quot;GHOUL and MORTAL&quot; called producer which allows your ghoul or human bloodbonded servant to produce twice as much vitae for you than the average Joe. That merit would make absolutely no sense to be in the book at all, or at very least THAT section of it, if you couldnt feed off a ghoul. Also that merit heavily heavily implies that when you do drink from a ghoul, you take their blood and leave their vitae reserve alone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Producer (\u2022)<br /> You may suffer a medical condition that means you produce<br /> a higher blood volume, or suffer from a thickening of the blood<br /> caused by too many red blood cells. Or your condition may be<br /> completely mystical and never show up under a microscope.<br /> However it manifests, you produce extra Vitae when a Kindred<br /> drinks from you.<br /> Prerequisite: Human or Ghoul<br /> Effect: For every point of lethal damage caused by feeding,<br /> Kindred gain two Vitae from your character.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you download the most recent version of the file, you will see that the only Prerequisite is Human, and ghouls cannot get it.<br /> <br /> Or look here.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/3FnWEXJ.pngp\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-30-2017, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T12:32:59-08:00","id":1164019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163925#post1163925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What was said above. Dhampiri do not have Disciplines, they have the fact that the very nature of being life born from death means they all have Fate Itself as their godparent. They have Twists, somewhat conceptual control over destiny, and besides their Beast being a second Vice that only rears its head when the dhampir is stressed, they all have a third Anchor, Destiny. Which they get Willpower from pursuing or actively thwarting, with both achievement and utter denial of resulting in a full refresh.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's unusual. I don't recall fate ever being a notable concept in Requiem or really anything like a force that related to Kindred and their ilk, nevermind Capital-F Fate. Doesn't sound like what I expected, I thought they'd be more... stuck in an uncomfortable middle, not-quite-vampiric offspring caught between their essential living nature and inhuman predatorial urges and powers.<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily bad that Dhampiri have a unique thing that distinguishes them from their origins, but it sticks out. Reserving proper judgement until I can read the material myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:04:08-08:00","id":1164032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164019#post1164019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's unusual. I don't recall fate ever being a notable concept in Requiem or really anything like a force that related to Kindred and their ilk, nevermind Capital-F Fate.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Strix have had disaster-sense since at least Wicked Dead, a core covenant's signature magical ability is based around the concept of mystically-binding blood oaths, and 2e's dhampir literally cannot be conceived without a purpose. The distinction between &quot;Capital-F Fate&quot; and &quot;pervasive supernatural force with an agenda&quot; is broadly academic when it comes to vampirism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:52:44-08:00","id":1164046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164019#post1164019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's unusual. I don't recall fate ever being a notable concept in Requiem or really anything like a force that related to Kindred and their ilk, nevermind Capital-F Fate. Doesn't sound like what I expected, I thought they'd be more... stuck in an uncomfortable middle, not-quite-vampiric offspring caught between their essential living nature and inhuman predatorial urges and powers.<br /> <br /> It's not necessarily bad that Dhampiri have a unique thing that distinguishes them from their origins, but it sticks out. Reserving proper judgement until I can read the material myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Satchel said, the Strix are linked to omens, which is generally what the dhampiri have power over. Fate is the source of their powers, but to a dhampir, it really doesn't matter to them apart from &quot;Why the hell is my life a whirling tempest of weird?&quot; That doesn't mean they aren't creatures of prophecy, mind; the Sanctified revere and fear them as the shepherds of shepherds, the ones who pick off vampires who succumb to corruption. But really, dhampiri care less about whether the stars are right rather than whether they can avoid being shot and/or enslaved because they are also an unhappy medium between living and dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:57:29-08:00","id":1164048,"title":"","content":"The disaster sense did belatedly occur to me, but overall the link sounds a bit... tenuous? The Strix have always had a very grim connection to omens, but that ability is practically a one-off in their bag of wicked tricks that speak much more directly to their nature as shadowy embodiments of cold, alien and envious hungers. The blood oaths of the Invictus don't sound connected to a broader comprehensible concept of fate, but rather one of the two core ideas in the powers of vampires, that <i>blood calls to blood</i> and those connections have occult significance that irrevocably brings things together; Mage's understanding of Fate as inclusive of such connections, magical promises, and the course of destiny and probabilities as one and the same, should probably not be considered of primary importance to something in Vampire The Requiem that concerns itself most of all.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs requiring a purpose behind their conception sounds more on point, but I can't really speak properly for the whole without reading the book. So I'm stuck analyzing the information that is being shared with a merely rational eye founded on printed precedents.<br /> <br /> And right now, it strikes me as inelegant that the book would nominate Fate in such a discrete fashion (even if only for the reader) to approach the defining weirdness-magnet nature of what one could call miraculously unlikely freaks born from weirdly auspicious circumstances, when the term includes implications that don't hold much water in the solo context of Requiem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-30-2017, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T13:59:16-08:00","id":1164051,"title":"","content":"How do you pronounce this, anyways?<br /> <br /> Is it 'Damn-peer?'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:13:53-08:00","id":1164056,"title":"","content":"Dam-pi-er<br /> They are Demi (half) vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:25:03-08:00","id":1164060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164048#post1164048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The disaster sense did belatedly occur to me, but overall the link sounds a bit... tenuous? The Strix have always had a very grim connection to omens, but that ability is practically a one-off in their bag of wicked tricks that speak much more directly to their nature as shadowy embodiments of cold, alien and envious hungers.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an aspect of their powerset that was explicitly able to be expanded further. &quot;Messing with fate&quot; commonly translates to &quot;supernatural meddling with an entity's reaction to and influence upon the path of least resistance.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The blood oaths of the Invictus don't sound connected to a broader comprehensible concept of fate, but rather one of the two core ideas in the powers of vampires, that <i>blood calls to blood</i> and those connections have occult significance that irrevocably brings things together </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much the whole of almost any given gameline's definition of &quot;fate&quot; \u2014 connected things influence each other and benefits come with costs that may be mitigated in certain circumstances. Gaining something comes with losing something else or gaining something different, and your relationships affect your existence within the wider framework of the supernatural world \u2014 Changeling makes that the most directly evident, but it's a concept that's present in the wider context of the Chronicles of Darkness in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage's understanding of Fate as inclusive of such connections, promises, and the course of destiny and probabilities as one and the same, should probably not be considered of primary importance to something in Vampire The Requiem that concerns itself most of all. </div> </div> </div>Rose has pointed out before that Kindred are magical creatures, despite Vampire generally avoiding using that term specifically to avoid conflation with Mage. The clans have curses and occult qualities, blood sorcery works better along a vampire's sympathies, and the Requiem in general plays on as an eerie neighbor to History, that stage of stages that circumstance and civilization provide to corral the Beast.<br /> <br /> &quot;Things are going to (at least 'try' to) Happen&quot; is what the dhampir interaction with &quot;Fate&quot; amounts to, and their Destiny is literally derived from what their vampire parent conceived them for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:29:09-08:00","id":1164062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164056#post1164056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dam-pi-er<br /> They are Demi (half) vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>So why not dampire?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:44:24-08:00","id":1164068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164062#post1164062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So why not dampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it\u2019s not right. It\u2019s Damn-Peir. You were right. Source: <a href=\"https://youtu.be/y4rQvbkqgR8\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/y4rQvbkqgR8</a>. Other terms for the same thing are: dhampyre (Damn-pi-er), dhamphir (Damn-fear), and dhampyr (same as the original). So really what ever you feel like if you use the right spelling. Source: Wikipedia\u2019s first source.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:51:13-08:00","id":1164070,"title":"","content":"It's not &quot;dampire&quot; because &quot;dampire&quot; looks stupid. It sounds like a wet vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T14:56:34-08:00","id":1164074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164070#post1164070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like a wet vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I asked how it was pronounced. I was guessing they didn't decide 'lets make it look ambiguously foreign, but sound silly.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:02:51-08:00","id":1164078,"title":"","content":"So I gave a quick look to the book. Looks nice. Haven't expected getting a new Lost Clan in it. I also wonder on how it looks like the Lance's view of Dhampirs in the book is 180 degrees than what was presented in Wicked Dead. I also kinda miss the whole &quot;Dhampirs are being born from a union of a vampire and mortal, no matter biological compatibility- cause occult, fuck science&quot;, but it is not something which would require me to work extra hard to change. Still, I am waiting to give it a more, in depth read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T15:34:11-08:00","id":1164087,"title":"","content":"My skepticism with that degree of equivalency, Satchel, is that Vampire The Requiem has only approached the topic through the idea of it essentially being easier to affect things that are connected through the symbolic substance that empowers and feeds Kindred, all else secondary because even if one can extrapolate the wider symbolism, this does not mean every game cares about it in the same way, nor should they. This is not to the exclusion of vampires being magical, because of course they are, but blood sympathy has not been presented as relating to the more ubiquitous meanings of fate up to this point, nor been greately suggestive of that bereft of a deeper analysis.<br /> <br /> I'm splitting hairs at this point though, so I apologize for going on a possibly inappropriate estimation of the content.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:11:10-08:00","id":1164090,"title":"","content":"Odd question, but having only just finished the dhampir chapter in the first quick readthrough, I appear to have missed something.<br /> <br /> Namely, what happens when dhampir is Embraced (aside from Doom upon the Sire, if the Half-Damned wills it)? Obviously you add the Vampire template, but certain things (merits, twists, themes, malisons, destiny) are a matter to consider. Dropping the third anchor, and Sanctity of merits covers some of it to be sure, but...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:23:07-08:00","id":1164093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164087#post1164087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My skepticism with that degree of equivalency, Satchel, is that Vampire The Requiem has only approached the topic through the idea of it essentially being easier to affect things that are connected through the symbolic substance that empowers and feeds Kindred, all else secondary because even if one can extrapolate the wider symbolism, this does not mean every game cares about it in the same way, nor should they.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a known quality of vampires that the themes and trends of their nature affect and are affected by their environment and associates, either through the Vitae or through the connections and vessels that contain and convey it. This isn't incompatible with vampires caring about how people behave and how the world changes because of it \u2014 quite the opposite, even if it seldom uses the word &quot;fate&quot; outside of esoteric contexts.<br /> <br /> Disciplines and their less refined roots can affect minds and the material world, and blood sorcery like that which most commonly empowers a vampire to spawn a dhampir expands that influence considerably. The circumstances of a dhampir's birth are stamped into their psychology and their powers engage with &quot;fate&quot; through connections and prediction as readily as Auspex and oaths do \u2014 Twists and Malisons work through conscious and unconscious exertion and plain blood-sacrifice, and the Destiny of a half-vampire is a piece of their mental makeup borne out of their being made for a purpose and growing stronger by engaging with that fact.<br /> <br /> It's the prosaic form of &quot;Fate&quot; with a side possibility of magic powers that relate to things people usually think of in regard to the mystical form of the concept \u2014 dhampir can read the future in entrails and prophetic dreams and declare themselves the nemeses and blood-siblings of chosen subjects in their more magical modes of activity, and their less deliberate abilities manifest as themed alignment with supernatural powers and dreadful circumstances based on their parent's clan and their subsequent development.<br /> <br /> It's fate in the sense of hard and easy choices presenting themselves to the supernaturally-touched, specifically as adjacent to the curse-heavy nature of vampirism. It's fate in the same sense that vampires are doomed to grow apart from humanity and become weird monsters in the night as that happens. Being born into a certain degree of bad luck and bad blood generally calls your lot in life into question in a way that dying hungry doesn't. This is something the children of vampires have to deal with more directly than vampires themselves do, because &quot;bad things happen around me&quot; is a little harder to brush off when you making them happen on purpose or in an atavistic fugue is an excuse that your dad has and you don't. This is fate in the sense of Circumstances Somewhat Beyond Your Control, as viewed by a type of person who quite likely has an eye on the entire class of inveterate supernatural meddlers who made them as they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T16:57:50-08:00","id":1164096,"title":"","content":"I would like to retort to the new information you're giving me, but I'm still working with incomplete context, so citing X and Y examples of how they engage with the magicness of blood in the original topic puts me a bit on the spot! This is why it's not wise to argue extensively without a more complete grasp on the topic.<br /> <br /> I can't say it is terribly convincing to reference increasingly figurative interpretations of fate where it shapes the life of a Dhampir though. That's more distracting than the part where you point out Twists and Malisons work through blood-sacrifice and they have powers based on their relation to the clan of their vampiric parent and asserting bonds through relations of blood as a mystic medium. The former is diverging to very general kinds of statement that you could apply to any supernatural with difficulties inherent by biology or circumstance, and the latter is explaining how they actually engage with one of the two main motifs of Kindred supernatural power.<br /> <br /> For that it's worth, I appreciate the time spent working to disabuse me of incomplete notions, but I don't think I can add anything else at this point in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-30-2017, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T17:34:25-08:00","id":1164102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164096#post1164096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't say it is terribly convincing to reference increasingly figurative interpretations of fate where it shapes the life of a Dhampir though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just narrow it down to this: What are you proposing to be a <i>non-</i>figurative interpretation of fate?<br /> <br /> A character who lives with weird shitty luck due to being born from the plans and loins of a monster is going to have a different perspective on words like &quot;destiny&quot; than a character whose conscious existence is undergirded with desperation held at bay through stolen life and the endurance of the unliving.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fate&quot; is an abstract concept that generally manifests in these dice-based storytelling games as narrative elements and/or changes to the default dice mechanics as appropriate to the supernatural force involved, and those manifestations are as indistinguishable from mundane coincidence to the casual observer in the game as those circumstances would be outside the framework of a story-game.<br /> <br /> In Vampire's case, those manifestations largely have to do with the living and the hungry dead that depend on them for sustenance and context, which looks different from one side of the fangs than the other. The focus does not have to exist across the entire gameline to be appropriate language for a specific phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T18:16:33-08:00","id":1164124,"title":"","content":"The idea of Fate as a discrete force that determines or influences what is likely to happen, which in this case looks over or relates to Dhampiri in some upkeeping manner that is tied to them having some of the powers they do. This is the suggestion Leliel's choice of words makes in the post that gave rise to my questioning.<br /> <br /> It is natural that someone with a life entrapped by circumstances beyond their control is going to have a particular view of destiny and predestination than people who have better control over their monstrous natures; that having different perspectives on those concepts determined by the limitations and afflictions of your life is <i>not</i> limited to Dhampiri in the Chronicles of Darkness (or even limited to supernatural creatures) is why I was claiming the train of thought was distracting from the point.<br /> <br /> The way the abstract notion of fate manifests in games is not overly complicated to understand, and of course it's going to be poorly understood as distinct from mundance coincidence to someone who doesn't have the awareness or knowledge to be able to suppose otherwise. The thing that was leaving me scratching my head was not a lack of understanding that things work like this. I was finding it strange because <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163925#post1163925\">this post</a> seems to describe the influence of fate on a Dhampir in a very <i>non</i>-figurative way, and attribute some qualities of their existence to it (irrespective of whether or not they know this as the reader does), as opposed to anything more directly relevant to the motifs of Kindred.<br /> <br /> And now I'm realizing that may have been my misunderstanding in reading Leliel literally. I can't really excuse myself if that's the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T20:37:03-08:00","id":1164168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164124#post1164124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing that was leaving me scratching my head was not a lack of understanding that things work like this. I was finding it strange because <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163925#post1163925\">this post</a> seems to describe the influence of fate on a Dhampir in a very <i>non</i>-figurative way, and attribute some qualities of their existence to it (irrespective of whether or not they know this as the reader does), as opposed to anything more directly relevant to the motifs of Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, no, Lel was being poetic in roughly the same way the chapter is about the fact that dhampir tend to pick up protections from and affinities for supernatural powers and natural circumstances that align with the themes of their parent's clan, that player use of Twists does not always translate to character invocation of those powers in the fiction, and that the basic Universal Dhampir Powers package includes getting Omen Sensitivity and Thief of Fate for free as part of the same umbrella quality that gives them Destiny as a weird hybrid Aspiration/Anchor Trait. Being a dhampir means having kind of a complicated life in a way that's easy to analogize to the Kindred's paranoid musings about whether the Curse has an agenda.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T22:39:27-08:00","id":1164182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164090#post1164090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Odd question, but having only just finished the dhampir chapter in the first quick readthrough, I appear to have missed something.<br /> <br /> Namely, what happens when dhampir is Embraced (aside from Doom upon the Sire, if the Half-Damned wills it)? Obviously you add the Vampire template, but certain things (merits, twists, themes, malisons, destiny) are a matter to consider. Dropping the third anchor, and Sanctity of merits covers some of it to be sure, but...</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't be Embraced (Dhampir Character Creation, p. 29).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-30T22:41:09-08:00","id":1164183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164078#post1164078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I gave a quick look to the book. Looks nice. Haven't expected getting a new Lost Clan in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>More than one, when you give it an in-depth read - I count at least three, two we get some detail on, one is an off-hand reference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T01:42:38-08:00","id":1164201,"title":"","content":"One thing with the book sort of confused me and left me sleepless for a while until I found a way to justify it within the core rulebook, but I want other peoples input on it.<br /> <br /> In the book, p. 90, it says that &quot;Mekhet create ghouls for one purpose: an eventual Embrace into the clan&quot; and it's stated on other pages (for example the Lancea and Ordo) that vampires aren't against the idea to embrace ghouls. <br /> <br /> Now, I thought: why Embrace someone that has a full Vinculum to you and most likely is also a Vitae Addict? Wouldn't that be bit of a problem?<br /> <br /> I always assumed that Vinculum and Addiction stayed with you after the Embrace. I guess one can argue that death solves the Vinculum and that the Embrace can be a resolution for the Addiction Condition(as in a loss of Integrity).<br /> <br /> What are your thought on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23564-elesadi","name":"Elesadi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23564_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T02:11:45-08:00","id":1164205,"title":"","content":"Ghouls getting embraced has been a thing since, like, forever. Clearly the issue is not an insurmountable one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T02:18:28-08:00","id":1164207,"title":"","content":"Vitae addiction could be a bit of a problem, but why wouldn't you want your childer to be blood bonded? Makes them less rebellious. Vinculum can be a hassle, but mostly if you don't have much control over the bonded party so they have time to act on the less desirable impulses they may get.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T02:22:37-08:00","id":1164208,"title":"","content":"I would avoid embracing someone with Vitae Adiction because it increases the chance that they will Frenzy and if you needed Vinculum to keep someone loyal you probably don't want to make them a full kindred.<br /> On the Dhampir subject could someone clarify for me do they use willpower to fuel their abilities? No one has mentioned a fuel stat for them so I assume so. I'm also curious about how much their vampire parent effects them? Do they come in 5 flavered like the clans, do they have something akin to the Tast of merits or are they mechanicly the same?<br /> On the subject of the Tast of merits do we get more must be a ghoul of clan X options?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:17:47-08:00","id":1164220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164208#post1164208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would avoid embracing someone with Vitae Adiction because it increases the chance that they will Frenzy and if you needed Vinculum to keep someone loyal you probably don't want to make them a full kindred.<br /> On the Dhampir subject could someone clarify for me do they use willpower to fuel their abilities? No one has mentioned a fuel stat for them so I assume so. I'm also curious about how much their vampire parent effects them? Do they come in 5 flavered like the clans, do they have something akin to the Tast of merits or are they mechanicly the same?<br /> On the subject of the Tast of merits do we get more must be a ghoul of clan X options?</div> </div> </div> </div>A dhampir's vampire parent influences their Themes (the thematic situations in which they can use Twists), their Affliction (the dark part of their nature that manifests when they exhaust themselves using their supernatural abilities), and the Doom they inflict on any vampire who feeds from them.<br /> <br /> Some Twists don't require fuelling, some require spending Willpower, and some require drinking a vampire's Vitae. Malisons require the dhampir to deliberately inflict some degree of damage on themselves to work.<br /> <br /> No 'Must be a ghoul of X' Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:25:36-08:00","id":1164221,"title":"","content":"Curious just bought PDF, but what does Charry DO?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T04:45:36-08:00","id":1164223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164220#post1164220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A dhampir's vampire parent influences their Themes (the thematic situations in which they can use Twists), their Affliction (the dark part of their nature that manifests when they exhaust themselves using their supernatural abilities), and the Doom they inflict on any vampire who feeds from them.<br /> <br /> Some Twists don't require fuelling, some require spending Willpower, and some require drinking a vampire's Vitae. Malisons require the dhampir to deliberately inflict some degree of damage on themselves to work.<br /> <br /> No 'Must be a ghoul of X' Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, so who your daddy is changes when you can use your powers? Makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T06:19:29-08:00","id":1164241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164221#post1164221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious just bought PDF, but what does Charry DO?</div> </div> </div> </div>Helps deal with the fact that revenants lose the entire contents of their Vitae pool upon waking by giving them ways to store or retain some of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T06:23:08-08:00","id":1164242,"title":"","content":"I'm in love with the ghouls chapter. I noticed some Tokyo Ghoul got in there too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The little bits of fiction throughout are excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T06:40:30-08:00","id":1164247,"title":"","content":"so after giving it some thought, I considered an option of making a personal review thread for the book (in the style of &quot;LostLight reads Half Damned&quot;, and I wanted ti check if there will be an interest in such thread before going through the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T07:54:46-08:00","id":1164266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elesadi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164201#post1164201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing with the book sort of confused me and left me sleepless for a while until I found a way to justify it within the core rulebook, but I want other peoples input on it.<br /> <br /> In the book, p. 90, it says that &quot;Mekhet create ghouls for one purpose: an eventual Embrace into the clan&quot; and it's stated on other pages (for example the Lancea and Ordo) that vampires aren't against the idea to embrace ghouls.<br /> <br /> Now, I thought: why Embrace someone that has a full Vinculum to you and most likely is also a Vitae Addict? Wouldn't that be bit of a problem?<br /> <br /> I always assumed that Vinculum and Addiction stayed with you after the Embrace. I guess one can argue that death solves the Vinculum and that the Embrace can be a resolution for the Addiction Condition(as in a loss of Integrity).<br /> <br /> What are your thought on this?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My take on the matter. When you die it breaks the blood bond. The magic or metaphysical power or whatever bond you had would extinguish when the life is snuffed out of you. Just like many of the powers end with the coming of the sun, many powers also end with your death. Whatever pull is lost.<br /> <br /> I also believe that your death would end the addiction as well for two reasons. One you are born again. Everything living in you died and you have utterly changed. Cancer stops, disease ends, your cravings change. Sure you would remember how amazing it was, but you have other hungers you need to deal with and fight with now. You have a beast inside you altering your very core. ( That memory might be enough for you to want to start again. Addicts struggle to remain sober on a daily basis even if they have been sober for years )<br /> <br /> Second, ( like you mentioned) Mechanically Persistent Addicted condition ends when you lose a dot of integrity/humanity. Mechanically when you turn, you lose all your integrity dots and replace them with 7 humanity. Even if you were at 2 integrity you come back with 7 humanity. So mechanically, you are fulfilling the resolution for that condition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164208#post1164208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would avoid embracing someone with Vitae Adiction because it increases the chance that they will Frenzy and if you needed Vinculum to keep someone loyal you probably don't want to make them a full kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both of these are Subjective. Your vampires might avoid such things for moral reasons, but there is nothing in the core rules ( that I know of.. I am slow reading this book in the entirety ) that says an addict is more likely to frenzy. There is a roll to resist indulging, but nothing is mentioned for a frenzy. If there is a negative at all it is a subjective, case by case Story teller choice. <br /> <br /> The Blood Bond again, is a subjective matter. It is mentioned that vampires do it to other vampires, so changing someone that was bonded is again a subjective call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 12-01-2017, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:03:02-08:00","id":1164273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164247#post1164247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so after giving it some thought, I considered an option of making a personal review thread for the book (in the style of &amp;quot;LostLight reads Half Damned&amp;quot;, and I wanted ti check if there will be an interest in such thread before going through the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to see something like that. It's not that I'm not already sold on the book. I am. Ghouls was the 1E book that finally sold my wife on Requiem, and led to our second or third longest running game ( in which her character played a member of a ghoul family that took herself off the breeding list by founding a breeding program for others, then traveled the world acting as ambassador to other ghoul families to bring them together for purposes of genetic diversity). I can't wait to see more of this one, but it will be awhile before I can get it myself. I would quite cheerfully read your review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:07:56-08:00","id":1164277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164247#post1164247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so after giving it some thought, I considered an option of making a personal review thread for the book (in the style of &quot;LostLight reads Half Damned&quot;, and I wanted ti check if there will be an interest in such thread before going through the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would be totally down with this. I love Let's Reads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T08:15:17-08:00","id":1164280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164247#post1164247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so after giving it some thought, I considered an option of making a personal review thread for the book (in the style of &quot;LostLight reads Half Damned&quot;, and I wanted ti check if there will be an interest in such thread before going through the effort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do, and if you won't mind, it could serve as a repository for reviews of bits by others, to avoid cluttering the forum. This thread has received fragmentary reviews but would require a careful read to really advise someone regarding the book.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T13:22:51-08:00","id":1164367,"title":"","content":"Embracing ghouls could of course go either way. If one is looking to sire progeny, it's not unreasonable to give them a taste first and see how the react.<br /> On the other hand if they're good at what they do, then why throw away a valuable asset, why release your prized 4H animal into the wild? If they're not good at it, then why are they still around? Or if the intention is to keep them bonded, then what is the role that they will fill better than if you changed nothing, and is it actually worth the extra problems that come with the Embrace?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-01T15:59:08-08:00","id":1164415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164168#post1164168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, no, Lel was being poetic in roughly the same way the chapter is about the fact that dhampir tend to pick up protections from and affinities for supernatural powers and natural circumstances that align with the themes of their parent's clan, that player use of Twists does not always translate to character invocation of those powers in the fiction, and that the basic Universal Dhampir Powers package includes getting Omen Sensitivity and Thief of Fate for free as part of the same umbrella quality that gives them Destiny as a weird hybrid Aspiration/Anchor Trait. Being a dhampir means having kind of a complicated life in a way that's easy to analogize to the Kindred's paranoid musings about whether the Curse has an agenda.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I feel slightly dumb now. So their powers are just based on their cursed birth and disadvantages they can inflict on others based on the inauspicious circumstances of their parentage, and they're tuned to a purpose enforced by the kindred which made them, whose lineage shapes the afflictions of their unnatural existence and how they in turn inflict misfortune on vampires who prey on them.<br /> <br /> Okay. I raise a brow in curiosity at Thief of Fate and the like, but this makes a lot more sense to me than whatever I initially got out of the choice of words in earlier posts. Their abilities are closely tied to the cursed and inauspicious aspect of vampires and interact with the wider world through that unfortunate lenses. That sounds like it connects well to the central motifs of vampiric power in the core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 12-01-2017, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T06:21:13-08:00","id":1164513,"title":"","content":"Reading through the book with more detail, and watching the errata thread...<br /> <br /> It really kind of feels like some of the writers couldn't be assed to figure out what game they were writing for. There are so many Classic World of Darkness &amp; 1E references that it's kind of ridiculous. Like, above and beyond using the wrong word for things, up to it actually affecting how certain mechanics are designed... =\\<br /> <br /> I'm still really happy with my purchase but this is disappointing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T08:10:04-08:00","id":1164533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164513#post1164513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the book with more detail, and watching the errata thread...<br /> <br /> It really kind of feels like some of the writers couldn't be assed to figure out what game they were writing for. There are so many Classic World of Darkness &amp; 1E references that it's kind of ridiculous. Like, above and beyond using the wrong word for things, up to it actually affecting how certain mechanics are designed... =\\<br /> <br /> I'm still really happy with my purchase but this is disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad I wasn't the only one that noticed that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T11:09:39-08:00","id":1164570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164513#post1164513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading through the book with more detail, and watching the errata thread...<br /> <br /> It really kind of feels like some of the writers couldn't be assed to figure out what game they were writing for. There are so many Classic World of Darkness &amp; 1E references that it's kind of ridiculous. Like, above and beyond using the wrong word for things, up to it actually affecting how certain mechanics are designed... =\\<br /> <br /> I'm still really happy with my purchase but this is disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which mechanics are you referring to? I'm not disagreeing, I just haven't had time to digest everything. I've been greatly enjoying the book so far, but the couple of time I've seen WofD instead of CofD did take me out of it a bit. The Werewolf section was a downer too, since it clearly wasn't talking about Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:33:22-08:00","id":1164639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1163864#post1163864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Revenants now have a merit called &quot;Fertile Vitae&quot; which lets them embrace other people as revenants. There are entire communities of them that operate mostly independently of kindred.<br /> <br /> I figured that would be a thing, because otherwise the idea that revenants are sort of proto-vampires doesn't work if they can't propagate themselves.<br /> <br /> There is a sidebar talking about a &quot;lost&quot; discipline that works the same as the revenant-only one, except that kinderd can also learn it, but I'm not sure why because half the powers would be useless to full vampires because they circumvent revenant-specific problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hello, I was the writer for the Chary Discipline, and as such, I feel like it'd be appropriate to explain Bereschligost, the Kindred equivalent.<br /> First off, I will note that it is a Discipline belonging to a clan that suffered from a curse of hibernation, and traditionally had a lot of elders, thus torpor was fairly common. Secondly, I'll point out that the clan lived in Siberia, where they often had to travel long distances to find human prey, hence the feeding on animals thing.<br /> There was originally a whole section on how the Kindred version differs from Chary, but I cut that before even submitting the first draft because it was an awful lot of word count to spend on mechanics that the subjects of the book could never use. Bereschligost is very similar to Chary, and I figured groups that wanted to bring in a &quot;live&quot; Mikhaili would modify Chary to suit that character's needs. It's not ideal, of course, but the Mikhaili exist in a pure page-count perspective as an accessory to Revenants. Even giving the basic mechanics was basically just self-indulgence, though I also thought the community would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> So, what does Bereschligost look like? Well, first off, all the individual powers would have new names, but since I don't remember what they were, let's ignore that for now.<br /> <br /> The first dot, Daily Bread, explicitly works for a torpid Kindred, too. You can store Vitae up to your dots in Blood Potency, not just one, and it's based on your Blood Potency when you fell asleep, not when you wake.up again.<br /> The second dot, Eating Flies, lets you drink blood from old corpses in addition to animals, or frozen blood without having to thaw it. You get one-fifth of the Vitae a fresh body would provide. Breaking Point ahoy, Humanity 4.<br /> The third dot, Predator As Prey, lets you drink Kindred blood without addiction. At Blood Potency 6, it's vinculum immunity instead. Note, however, the Willpower requirement - you can still bond a Mikhaili elder, you just need to torture them first. Note the Mikhaili backstory to see how this power worked out for them in the long run.<br /> <br /> The fourth and fifth dots are completely different powers from Chary altogether, and at that point, I'd already scrapped the section for word count, so all I have there are vague ideas. Dot 4 has something to do with the Predatory Aura, strengthening and weakening it to manipulate other vampires. Dot 5 improves the vampire's ability to Blood Bond, and also lets them keep ghouls without needing to feed them as often.<br /> <br /> So, well, Chary for Kindred! Not quite the same, but very close. Hope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T14:47:37-08:00","id":1164645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164639#post1164639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, I was the writer for the Chary Discipline, and as such, I feel like it'd be appropriate to explain Bereschligost, the Kindred equivalent.<br /> First off, I will note that it is a Discipline belonging to a clan that suffered from a curse of hibernation, and traditionally had a lot of elders, thus torpor was fairly common. Secondly, I'll point out that the clan lived in Siberia, where they often had to travel long distances to find human prey, hence the feeding on animals thing.<br /> There was originally a whole section on how the Kindred version differs from Chary, but I cut that before even submitting the first draft because it was an awful lot of word count to spend on mechanics that the subjects of the book could never use. Bereschligost is very similar to Chary, and I figured groups that wanted to bring in a &quot;live&quot; Mikhaili would modify Chary to suit that character's needs. It's not ideal, of course, but the Mikhaili exist in a pure page-count perspective as an accessory to Revenants. Even giving the basic mechanics was basically just self-indulgence, though I also thought the community would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> So, what does Bereschligost look like? Well, first off, all the individual powers would have new names, but since I don't remember what they were, let's ignore that for now.<br /> <br /> The first dot, Daily Bread, explicitly works for a torpid Kindred, too. You can store Vitae up to your dots in Blood Potency, not just one, and it's based on your Blood Potency when you fell asleep, not when you wake.up again.<br /> The second dot, Eating Flies, lets you drink blood from old corpses in addition to animals, or frozen blood without having to thaw it. You get one-fifth of the Vitae a fresh body would provide. Breaking Point ahoy, Humanity 4.<br /> The third dot, Predator As Prey, lets you drink Kindred blood without addiction. At Blood Potency 6, it's vinculum immunity instead. Note, however, the Willpower requirement - you can still bond a Mikhaili elder, you just need to torture them first. Note the Mikhaili backstory to see how this power worked out for them in the long run.<br /> <br /> The fourth and fifth dots are completely different powers from Chary altogether, and at that point, I'd already scrapped the section for word count, so all I have there are vague ideas. Dot 4 has something to do with the Predatory Aura, strengthening and weakening it to manipulate other vampires. Dot 5 improves the vampire's ability to Blood Bond, and also lets them keep ghouls without needing to feed them as often.<br /> <br /> So, well, Chary for Kindred! Not quite the same, but very close. Hope this helps!</div> </div> </div> </div>This is really cool! The Mikhaili are definitely going to be involved (in a small way) with the Requiem for Rome chronicle I've got cooking...<br /> <br /> Tbis isn't quite relevant to the discussion, but out of curiosity, what languages are Chary and Bereschligost from? I sort of ran through Google translate with my vague knowledge of Russian, but it didn't reveal much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:14:26-08:00","id":1164657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164570#post1164570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which mechanics are you referring to?</div> </div> </div> </div>Clan Impostor comes to mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:17:28-08:00","id":1164660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164639#post1164639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, well, Chary for Kindred! Not quite the same, but very close. Hope this helps!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the writeup! The Mikhaili were a really cool addition to Half-Damned, and I'd love to get a full, official version of them sometime. I like the idea of a clan that's adapted to a harsher, more rural and spread out situation than the ultra-urban Kindred we usually deal with. I also thought the idea of them being &quot;out-competed&quot; by the more familiar Gangrel moving in was a nice bit of natural selection added into our supernatural setting, and their fall \u2014 by doing exactly the wrong thing \u2014 serves as another great lesson for modern vampires looking at the big picture. (see also &quot;Strix, Julii and the&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:33:33-08:00","id":1164663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164645#post1164645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is really cool! The Mikhaili are definitely going to be involved (in a small way) with the Requiem for Rome chronicle I've got cooking...<br /> <br /> Tbis isn't quite relevant to the discussion, but out of curiosity, what languages are Chary and Bereschligost from? I sort of ran through Google translate with my vague knowledge of Russian, but it didn't reveal much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bereschligost is Russian, Chary is English.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164657#post1164657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clan Impostor comes to mind</div> </div> </div> </div>I assume you're referring to the Nosferatu reference? That doesn't refer to appearance, though certainly some Requiem Nosferatu look downright grody. It refers to the wrong and twisted way being around them feels. It's immediately obvious in a way none of the other clan banes manage to be. Hollow Mekhet would also go under that clause. I can assure you that the Merit was designed with the the Lonely Curse in mind.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164660#post1164660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you for the writeup! The Mikhaili were a really cool addition to Half-Damned, and I'd love to get a full, official version of them sometime. I like the idea of a clan that's adapted to a harsher, more rural and spread out situation than the ultra-urban Kindred we usually deal with. I also thought the idea of them being &quot;out-competed&quot; by the more familiar Gangrel moving in was a nice bit of natural selection added into our supernatural setting, and their fall \u2014 by doing exactly the wrong thing \u2014 serves as another great lesson for modern vampires looking at the big picture. (see also &quot;Strix, Julii and the&quot;)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like my little morality tale, there. I'll note that the story in Half-Damned is Kindred mythology, and things probably didn't go down quite as pat as the tale would have you believe.<br /> <br /> I've long wanted more stuff for rural Kindred, in both Masquerade and Requiem. This is one of my little stabs at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T15:45:44-08:00","id":1164668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164663#post1164663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I assume you're referring to the Nosferatu reference? That doesn't refer to appearance, though certainly some Requiem Nosferatu look downright grody. It refers to the wrong and twisted way being around them feels. It's immediately obvious in a way none of the other clan banes manage to be. Hollow Mekhet would also go under that clause. I can assure you that the Merit was designed with the the Lonely Curse in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the Lonely Curse specifically don't affect vampires, so Nosferatu wouldn't have much problem pretending they're another clan, except in the few cases they're meaningfully interacting with humans in the presence of other vampires. In my experience that's hardly a common occurrence, and quite easily circumvented if you insist on having a ghoul intermediary because you're above associating with the cattle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:04:31-08:00","id":1164676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164668#post1164668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the Lonely Curse specifically don't affect vampires, so Nosferatu wouldn't have much problem pretending they're another clan, except in the few cases they're meaningfully interacting with humans in the presence of other vampires. In my experience that's hardly a common occurrence, and quite easily circumvented if you insist on having a ghoul intermediary because you're above associating with the cattle.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bane does not apply mechanically, but is still distinctive. Yes, a Revenant can maintain a false identity if she wants by just staying in private and using intermediaries, but Clan Impostor is about acting normally as a member of the clan.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, even if the Nosferatu clan bane is in fact intended to be completely unnoticable to Kindred, all it takes to bring the charade crashing down is one ghoul or retainer to say, &quot;You know, that 'Haunt' is really not very haunting...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:07:09-08:00","id":1164678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164676#post1164676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The bane does not apply mechanically, but is still distinctive. Yes, a Revenant can maintain a false identity if she wants by just staying in private and using intermediaries, but Clan Impostor is about acting normally as a member of the clan.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, even if the Nosferatu clan bane is in fact intended to be completely unnoticable to Kindred, all it takes to bring the charade crashing down is one ghoul or retainer to say, &quot;You know, that 'Haunt' is really not very haunting...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that clan banes don't apply until your Humanity drops below 7, so it's not as if non-creepy nosferatu don't exist. And sure that all might draw suspicion over time but that seems like an IC reason to apply Sancity of merits to it, not a reason to prevent it from the get go as a physical impossibility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:12:35-08:00","id":1164679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164678#post1164678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's also the fact that clan banes don't apply until your Humanity drops below 7, so it's not as if non-creepy nosferatu don't exist. And sure that all might draw suspicion over time but that seems like an IC reason to apply Sancity of merits to it, not a reason to prevent it from the get go as a physical impossibility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't actually aware that clan banes stopped applying at high Humanity, so this is a good reason to amend the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:22:25-08:00","id":1164681,"title":"","content":"they don't stop happening at high humanity, clan banes just don't apply until you first drop to humanity 6 (you start at 7), but after you drop to humanity 6 and your clan bane takes effect you will always be effected by your clan bane, even if you rise you humanity to 7+ again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12845-ahather","name":"ahather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12845_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:22:48-08:00","id":1164683,"title":"","content":"It's not that they don't aply at high Humanity but that they don't emerge until Humanity 6 but then you're stuck with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:24:29-08:00","id":1164685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164679#post1164679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't actually aware that clan banes stopped applying at high Humanity, so this is a good reason to amend the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much that they don't apply at High Humanity, but they don't kick in until you drop below 7 the first time. If you raise it later, the curse still applies. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, you could argue that the clan bane doesn't have a mechanical effect after the first humanity drop, but the Haunt still feels &quot;creepy&quot; before it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T16:26:18-08:00","id":1164686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164679#post1164679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't actually aware that clan banes stopped applying at high Humanity, so this is a good reason to amend the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should we put this in the errata thread, then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T17:16:55-08:00","id":1164699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164686#post1164686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should we put this in the errata thread, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feel free. My suggested correction:<br /> <br /> &quot;While you can choose any clan to imitate, playing at being Nosferatu can suddenly become dangerous if you do not maintain at least the pretense of Humanity. A non-revenant vampire may also take this Merit, though it is less useful to them, and Haunts face the same obstacles in reverse as those who imitate them.&quot; Next paragraph, remove the last sentence entirely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23571,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","user":"Spider Queen","date":". 12-02-2017, 08:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen","name":"Spider Queen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T17:23:06-08:00","id":1164701,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to see the comparative strengths of the half damned vs. each other.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs have their own powers and can't learn Disciplines except Cruac with a three dot merit. Still between Cruac and Malisons they are potientally powerful Blood Sorcerers even if they have to injure themselves to do so (down side, they heal like humans). They are good at twisting fate as well.<br /> <br /> Ghouls are for the most part more powerful then Dampyr's having simular powers to Vampires, including healing themselves with Vitae, and using Disciplines, but can barely use Blood Sorcery at all. Downside most are slaves to Vampires.<br /> <br /> Reverents are still more powerful, but at the cost of being the hungiest, but they can feed on animals. I can see Reverents fleeing to literal farms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T17:59:03-08:00","id":1164709,"title":"","content":"As a random note, given the timing of this and the Changeling Kickstarter, has anyone else had the thought &quot;What happens when you turn a goblin fruit plant into a Mandragora&quot; yet?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T20:03:03-08:00","id":1164728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164709#post1164709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a random note, given the timing of this and the Changeling Kickstarter, has anyone else had the thought &amp;quot;What happens when you turn a goblin fruit plant into a Mandragora&amp;quot; yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>If only we had an upcoming Dark Era that featured both changelings and vampires...<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see dhampirs interacting with changelings and mummies. It strikes me there could be some good story fodder there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://