ame":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T20:41:42-08:00","id":1164732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spider Queen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164663#post1164663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm glad you like my little morality tale, there. I'll note that the story in Half-Damned is Kindred mythology, and things probably didn't go down quite as pat as the tale would have you believe.<br /> <br /> I've long wanted more stuff for rural Kindred, in both Masquerade and Requiem. This is one of my little stabs at that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really neat! Lost clans are always an interesting hook to build off of. Out of curiosity, do you have any thoughts as to when the Mikhaili were active and when they were driven to (near) extinction? <br /> <br /> **Furiously scribbles notes for Dark Eras 3**","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T12:59:10-08:00","id":1164861,"title":"","content":"does a revenant need Fertile Vitae to use &quot;Raise the Familiar&quot;? thought to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T11:47:59-08:00","id":1165105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1164732#post1164732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really neat! Lost clans are always an interesting hook to build off of. Out of curiosity, do you have any thoughts as to when the Mikhaili were active and when they were driven to (near) extinction?<br /> <br /> **Furiously scribbles notes for Dark Eras 3**</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you asked!<br /> <br /> [In one of several theories. Also edited noting <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23571-spider-queen\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23571\" data-vbnamecard=\"23571\">Spider Queen</a>'s earlier responses. As a direct comment, I do like the Revenant section! It's my favorite of the three.]<br /> <br /> The Huns (as they were known to the Romans, later), were evicted from what is now Western China about 200 BC, and chased west by Chinese generals to ensure they got good and far and didn't come back to harass the Han again. This initiated the Migration Period, as the Huns knocked into one people-group after another, setting them moving west and washing into Europe. I would pick this period, broadly, as when the Mikhaili were disturbed and eventually submerged by invaders.<br /> <br /> The Mikhaili would be from among the Slavic peoples who lived in the enormous forest band from Germany all the way to the Pacific Ocean. I'd place them mostly west of the Urals, however. North of them lay Finno-Ugric peoples, and south lay the Scythian plains and the great steppe and deserts of Central Asia.<br /> <br /> As an aside, the Slavic tribe of Novgorod invited Rurik (a viking, or varangian) in the late 9th century to be a king to rule and protect them. (I'm oversimplifying--it may have been a protection racket.) The end result was the conquering of a series of city-state kinglets scattered throughout the region, and several centuries of conflict that ended up, in time, placing Muscovy on top. Circling back to the Mikhaili, one wonders why it was then that Novgorod felt they were without rulership, hmm?<br /> <br /> I'd love migration period DE, but there is actually so little to base something on that you'd end up writing &gt;75% from whole cloth.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12493,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","user":"Khanwulf","date":". 12-04-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:10:44-08:00","id":1165296,"title":"","content":"I really get the feeling from this book that the writers don't understand what sets Requiem 2ed apart from 1ed, and Masquerade. It feels forced at times and puts a lot of overemphasis on the abusive nature of vampires and how shit they are, how the Half-Damned is so abused and neglected and, really put it, more hated then useful. Like Ghouls get so beaten by a thorny stick it's practically impossible to think how ghouls could be anywhere near useful with their mental och physical fuck-up-ness they all suffer. I did not expect to see this much abuse in requiem, i wouldn't even expect this from Sabbat or Camarilla elders en mass in V:tM. Where is the dynamics? Why is so much black and white? This book feels a lot more V:tM then it does V:tR:2ed. And beyond simple theme and mood about the setting, rules and shit seems to be mixed up.<br /> <br /> <br /> But a question about the specific rules about the vampire condition. I've always been under the impression that Blood Bonds stop working after death, e.g. the Embrace. However the old Ghoul book says i doesn't, and the forum recently said this to me, and it opened up some new thoughts and ideas that i actually has come to like. This book seems to remove this, by saying that Revenants loose Blood Bonds if they're uplifted to Kindred. Can't we get this a bit straight out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:06:40-08:00","id":1165347,"title":"","content":"Mm... so from what I've been hearing the last few days, this book probably isn't for me. I <i>adored</i> the tonal shift the 2e core took with vampires and ghouls, and one part of that is thanks to the spin of &quot;ghoul abuse happens, but is generally seen in Kindred society as roughly equivalent to attacking one's own foot&quot;. Still had strong, unsettling, possessive undertones that storytellers could play up if they wanted (&quot;you aren't just you anymore, you're my eyes and arms and voice in the daylight hours and you are bound to me by my Blood&quot; is pretty damn creepy in its own right), but it was strikingly - <i>pleasantly</i> - different from the &quot;mangy mutt on a short, rusty chain&quot; treatment that seemed the default in 1e. It sounds like this supplement (or at least sections of it) tossed that aside in favor of basically recreating some of the most uncomfortable parts of 1e's <i>Ghouls</i> book at <i>best</i>, or possibly even started treading the &quot;being a mortal sucks and you <i>will</i> be used up and tossed aside like a dollar store battery&quot; path that WoD seemed to favor and that ChroD has been pretty good at avoiding up until now.<br /> <br /> At this point I don't care as much if animal ghouls or mandragora have a presence, or that the dhampir got reworked to be more than just blood-soaked fly zappers. If the book isn't consistent with the gameline and edition it was written for (or even with itself if I'm hearing correctly) then I'm going to pass on it and keep my expectations low for the next supplement. I don't want to think it's going to turn into a trend, but between the response to this and my own feelings about <i>Thousand Years of Night</i> it feels like it might.<br /> <br /> To those of you who have and enjoy this book, I hope that it goes over well at your table regardless of if you're playing a character or creating NPCs with its rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T10:39:57-08:00","id":1165355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sconce</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165347#post1165347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm... so from what I've been hearing the last few days, this book probably isn't for me. I <i>adored</i> the tonal shift the 2e core took with vampires and ghouls, and one part of that is thanks to the spin of &quot;ghoul abuse happens, but is generally seen in Kindred society as roughly equivalent to attacking one's own foot&quot;. Still had strong, unsettling, possessive undertones that storytellers could play up if they wanted (&quot;you aren't just you anymore, you're my eyes and arms and voice in the daylight hours and you are bound to me by my Blood&quot; is pretty damn creepy in its own right), but it was strikingly - <i>pleasantly</i> - different from the &quot;mangy mutt on a short, rusty chain&quot; treatment that seemed the default in 1e. It sounds like this supplement (or at least sections of it) tossed that aside in favor of basically recreating some of the most uncomfortable parts of 1e's <i>Ghouls</i> book at <i>best</i>, or possibly even started treading the &quot;being a mortal sucks and you <i>will</i> be used up and tossed aside like a dollar store battery&quot; path that WoD seemed to favor and that ChroD has been pretty good at avoiding up until now.<br /> <br /> At this point I don't care as much if animal ghouls or mandragora have a presence, or that the dhampir got reworked to be more than just blood-soaked fly zappers. If the book isn't consistent with the gameline and edition it was written for (or even with itself if I'm hearing correctly) then I'm going to pass on it and keep my expectations low for the next supplement. I don't want to think it's going to turn into a trend, but between the response to this and my own feelings about <i>Thousand Years of Night</i> it feels like it might.<br /> <br /> To those of you who have and enjoy this book, I hope that it goes over well at your table regardless of if you're playing a character or creating NPCs with its rules.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What I am hoping for is that the developers, writers and editors will come on here and see the errata and flaws. It is still only in the PDF version and we know that with the core Blood and Smoke / vampire the requiem 2edition, there were still several major changes and edits. (such as the title of the book ) So hopefully the powers that be will fix this book before they send it to print on Demand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:06:59-08:00","id":1165367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165355#post1165355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I am hoping for is that the developers, writers and editors will come on here and see the errata</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165355#post1165355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and flaws.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking about the issues with tone and how this feels like a 1E or even CWoD book at times, I'm not holding my breath. At the end of the day, fixing these issues would be even more of a massive rewrite than fixing Beast was, and that itself brought a whole host of issues. <br /> <br /> I don't think it's reasonable to expect them to go that route with a supplement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T11:19:10-08:00","id":1165370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165367#post1165367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely happening.<br /> <br /> If we're talking about the issues with tone and how this feels like a 1E or even CWoD book at times, I'm not holding my breath. At the end of the day, fixing these issues would be even more of a massive rewrite than fixing Beast was, and that itself brought a whole host of issues.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's reasonable to expect them to go that route with a supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Boy I sure hope they see. This product seems rushed. <br /> <br /> And to the second point, it would not take that much work to spend some quality time with the document and think about the tone, the holes and questions raised by the material yet unanswered. Not as much as obtaining new text and new art would. This is also not a main splat-book; what we have now is a supplement's advance PDF that needs some love. I hope it gets that love.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:01:07-08:00","id":1165379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165370#post1165370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Boy I sure hope they see. This product seems rushed.<br /> <br /> And to the second point, it would not take that much work to spend some quality time with the document and think about the tone, the holes and questions raised by the material yet unanswered. Not as much as obtaining new text and new art would. This is also not a main splat-book; what we have now is a supplement's advance PDF that needs some love. I hope it gets that love.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly this forum is already doing a lot of the work for them on it...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:12:22-08:00","id":1165383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165379#post1165379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly this forum is already doing a lot of the work for them on it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hounestly, that\u2019s not really true. Certainly the problems are being pointed out, but very few people are giving solutions and even then, writing is hard and writing out the bad parts needs effort and thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13001-sdespencer","name":"SdeSpencer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:32:15-08:00","id":1165426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SdeSpencer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165383#post1165383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hounestly, that\u2019s not really true. Certainly the problems are being pointed out, but very few people are giving solutions and even then, writing is hard and writing out the bad parts needs effort and thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>First step to fixing any problem is identifying the problem. Or Pointing out the problems. The errata thread is pages long of people who aren't getting paid identifying errors that need to be fixed. <br /> <br /> As for your, &quot;writing is hard&quot; statement. The people who write these are professional writers. Any good professional writer shouldn't think it's too hard to overcome. Just like after having a teacher go through your essays and scribbling all sorts of corrections and pointing out parts that make no sense, it's easy enough to fix it after that. The writer already has the draft done, the mistakes pointed out, the goal, the purpose and Changing bits here and there, so it's coherent should be the easiest part of all. Granted. I can't speak for everyone, but I have taken a goodly amount of writing courses and taught a few, so this opinion is based on that and I am aware that everyone is different. <br /> <br /> I did not say all of the work. I am going to stick firm to my opinion that finding the mistakes is harder than fixing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:37:58-08:00","id":1165428,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hi, Danielle the developer here:</span></span> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A few notes on the tone of the book and the ghoul chapter in particular and the Clan Imposter Merit:<br /> <br /> The theme of this whole book was &quot;messy relationships.&quot; All the half-damned we see have complicated and messy relationships with vampires and each other. Dhampir were pure antagonists in 1e, hunting and murdering their vampire parents. In 2e we changed them to reflect that they may not hate or want to kill their parents, but being raised by vampires is likely to cause a lot of emotional baggage. But, that doesn't make them hate them, its just complicated. For revenants, they revere vampires. Those guys have the best life, and they even want to pretend to be them. Their relationships are also hard because they are trying to prove themselves to the All Night Society while skirting along its edges. Ghouls (which I get into much greater detail below) are addicts living two lives. Balancing both those lives are complicated and messy, and really it's hard to keep your normal life when your vampire life is just so much cooler.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Let's address the Clan Imposter Merit. When we were coming up with the ability for Revenants to pretend to be full vampires, we realized that these guys were going to be playing a long game. While yes, the Lonely Curse doesn't show up until the Nosferatu's Humanity drops to 6, as soon as that happens, the gig is up. Also, just because the mechanical penalty doesn't apply to Touchstones or Vampires doesn't mean that these people don't see the curse, it just means they ignore it for social reasons. Vampires aren't blind to a Nosferatu's weirdness, they just don't care as much as humans do. But they would certainly wonder why that person telling everyone they were a Nosferatu didn't have the same weirdness going on that other Nosferatu have. Does that make more sense? Also, I'm not opposed to making a slight change to reflect that it might just be harder or dangerous to impersonate a Nosferatu.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As for the ghoul chapter, I'd like to share some thoughts that went into writing that chapter. When writing the outline for the chapter, I wanted the writers to consider the complicated relationships that go into being blood bound to someone, and living as their servant. I wanted to touch on the personal horror of addiction and what kinds of problems addiction (blood) and the feelings of overwhelming love (viniculum) can have on a person. Ghouls are people who do whatever they can for a fix, and love the person they are getting their fix from, even as they maybe resent the fact that they have the fix in the first place and also love the power that comes with it. It's very complicated and messy. This shadows every other relationship they have, and I felt like it wouldn't be doing the ghouls any justice if we didn't cover all those messy aspects. And Requiem is all about the messy personal relationships in our character's lives. While we do have a couple of sections on how those kinds of relationships can look like abuse, we also spend a great deal of time talking about how the ghoul's life is more complicated than that. Heck, there's even a sidebar about not really bringing the abuse stuff into game. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1164313-let-s-read-half-damned?p=1165318#post1165318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A third of the book is dedicated to ghouls, but unless you want to expand on the ghoul appendix in the core book it's not really useful.</div> </div> </div> </div> </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This is from another thread, but honestly it's a true assessment. We took a lot of the story seeds and ideas for the ghoul appendix in the 2e book and expanded on them as themes for this chapter. So if you're looking for an expansion of that appendix, this is really that. </span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:39:27-08:00","id":1165429,"title":"","content":"I seriously doubt we're going to get any major rewrites. The only time that has happened was with BtP when we got a preview PDF. This is the advanced PDF after going through art direction and layouts. Even a single line more or less can get the entire layout to shift from that point forward, requiring whole new layout and indexing phases before the PDF can go to print. That's why the &quot;errata&quot; version almost exclusively contains grammatical and spelling fixes along with a few minor rules/fluff fixes that are limited to a single sentence.<br /> <br /> I get why OP does this, but I still hate the model. Especially since OP doesn't do erratas after the book has gone to print that could potentially fix a lot of inconsistencies and unexplained rules. I don't expect them to update in the actual books since you can't update already sold physical copies, but they won't even do them as separate free downloads. Any erratas for 2e you've seen are the results of the writers spending their unpaid, free time.<br /> <br /> <br /> All in all this (by which I mean Half-Damned; not necessarily the business practices) makes me dread Spilled Blood. Lost clans and alternate bloodlines? That'd be the most hyped VtR supplement for me, but with the mostly anticlimactic Thousand Years of Night, and the mess that is Half-Damned I'm really worried they're going to screw up what could easily be my most favourite VtR book.<br /> I really, really hope any of the devs sees this message and rethinks their development process. VtR core is a really solid book, and if Spilled Blood can hold the same level of quality I'd be extremely grateful.<br /> <br /> Rant over for me. Many other people has also stated their opinions about Half-Damned, and I don't want it to become a witch hunt rather than a statement of my opinion, so I probably won't write much more about this topic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: I didn't see Danielle's post until after posting this one. This post is not a direct reply to that post. The first part is a reply to the chances of getting substantial rewrite, and the second are my own general opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 12-05-2017, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T14:57:55-08:00","id":1165435,"title":"","content":"I for one really loved the book. It did everything I wanted it to. The ghouls chapter in particular was fantastic, so kudos to your writers as well as yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:34:42-08:00","id":1165445,"title":"","content":"Glad to see someone likes it, I'm waiting for the physical copy before buying it so hopefully by the time that comes out I'll be able to get balanced feedback on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:39:15-08:00","id":1165447,"title":"","content":"While VtR hasn't been at the top of Chronicles game's I've followed. It strikes me that characterizing any messy power dynamics in Vampire the Requiem as &quot;Just like Vampire the Masquerade.&quot; as making a lazy argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:44:11-08:00","id":1165448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165429#post1165429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get why OP does this, but I still hate the model. <b>Especially since OP doesn't do erratas after the book has gone to print that could potentially fix a lot of inconsistencies and unexplained rules.</b> I don't expect them to update in the actual books since you can't update already sold physical copies, but they won't even do them as separate free downloads. Any erratas for 2e you've seen are the results of the writers spending their unpaid, free time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Question: do any other of the current TRPG companies do this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T15:44:37-08:00","id":1165449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165447#post1165447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While VtR hasn't been at the top of Chronicles game's I've followed. It strikes me that characterizing any messy power dynamics in Vampire the Requiem as &quot;Just like Vampire the Masquerade.&quot; as making a lazy argument.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who's making that argument?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","user":"Poseur","date":". 12-05-2017, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:03:50-08:00","id":1165453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165448#post1165448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: do any other of the current TRPG companies do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wizards of the Coast, Fantasy Flight, Steve Jackson Games, and Chaosium. They're all certainly bigger than The Onyx Path (at least the former two, don't know too much about the latter tbh), but even if they weren't doing erratas I'd still find it a bad practice. Everyone jumping off a cliff doesn't make jumping off a cliff a good idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:21:54-08:00","id":1165458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165453#post1165453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wizards of the Coast, Fantasy Flight, Steve Jackson Games, and Chaosium. They're all certainly bigger than The Onyx Path (at least the former two, don't know too much about the latter tbh), but even if they weren't doing erratas I'd still find it a bad practice. Everyone jumping off a cliff doesn't make jumping off a cliff a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly this is one of those things that's hard to really discuss without knowing the full details on the hows and whys OPP runs the way they do in comparison to other TRPG companies. And even then, they might not even be at liberty to say why they do things the way they do for legal reasons. For all we know, there could be a perfectly logical reason why OPP runs things the way they are in consideration for whatever limitations they have on themselves.<br /> <br /> (I should also remind that WotC is a weird case considering that they apparently still don't believe in making official PDFs for current edition D&amp;D books available and are still mostly reliant on physical releases so...eh)<br /> <br /> Even then, we do have the pitfall of how people feel that they shouldn't need that extra errata document in the first place. That they would rather it already be printed in the book to begin with...which means waiting on 2nd printings, 3rd printings, etc. And since no one knows when those other releases are coming out it can be still a helluva wait.<br /> <br /> Besides, it could be way worse. It could be how Catalyst Game Labs handles errata for Shadowrun...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:40:58-08:00","id":1165462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165428#post1165428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Hi, Danielle the developer here:</span></span> </div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Danielle - I think it's pretty cool that you've jumped in here to provide your insights. Despite the criticisms, I would like to reiterate that I do really like what you &amp; the writers have produced here. These Dhampir <i>are</i> absolutely a huge step up from the version in Night Horrors and I'll be incorporating at least one into my campaigns within the next couple of weeks.<br /> <br /> More than specific issues (such as Clan Impostor) I think the main disappointment experienced by myself and a handful of others is the general tone with which the book seems to treat vampires and how much it differs from the way they are presented in the 2E core. Half-Damned seems to refocus on vampires as abusive monsters incapable of feeling which was an angle that was very much lessened with Blood &amp; Smoke.<br /> <br /> This focus (which seems more fitting with first edition), coupled with the sprinkling of terminology from a different game altogether (CWoD) leads to a total picture that feels, to some people, like something that's not really written for the new edition.<br /> <br /> Is this something you can speak to? Is the lens we're seeing vampires through a result of viewing them through the eyes of the Half-Damned themselves? Is it an intentional thematic departure? An accident? Something else entirely?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T16:49:57-08:00","id":1165464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165462#post1165462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Danielle - I think it's pretty cool that you've jumped in here to provide your insights. <b>Despite the criticisms, I would like to reiterate that I do really like what you &amp; the writers have produced here</b>. These Dhampir <i>are</i> absolutely a huge step up from the version in Night Horrors and I'll be incorporating at least one into my campaigns within the next couple of weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to reinforce this first bit as well. Other people have covered my concerns about tone, so I don't need to beat the (un)dead horse. I just want to say that while I share those concerns, that doesn't mean I don't like this book. Dhampirs will be a definite thing in my campaign, more lost clans are always welcome, and there are some pretty awesome ideas to pull from. Its still a solid book. The tonal dissonance... is a little jarring in places, and it knocks Half-Damned down a peg from being an outstanding addition to Requiem, but that doesn't change the fact I have enjoyed it for the most part and will use it when I get a chance. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T19:12:00-08:00","id":1165495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165462#post1165462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this something you can speak to? Is the lens we're seeing vampires through a result of viewing them through the eyes of the Half-Damned themselves? Is it an intentional thematic departure? <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you've hit a nail on a head here. This book is focused almost entirely on the experience of the half-damned characters. So their PoV colors how we talk about their relationships and how they feel about vampires.<br /> <br /> Our aim was to present these as playable characters, and so these are the character mindsets that we wrote in. I can understand the feeling that this departs from the norm, but part of the vampire's horror is how she ruins other people's lives by being too extra. So those people are bound to feel messy and complicated feelings about the vampire, and resentment is high up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Danielle Lauzon, Requiem Developer, Storypath Guru, freelance writer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6155-impernious","name":"impernious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T04:11:44-08:00","id":1165546,"title":"","content":"What about the way werewolves are pictured though? It seems like they are presented more like Apocalypse's than Forsaken, least alone the 2nd edition version, for what people commented. Is that right? Is this also a matter of unreliable narrator and outsider point of view?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T08:20:21-08:00","id":1165577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165495#post1165495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've hit a nail on a head here. This book is focused almost entirely on the experience of the half-damned characters. So their PoV colors how we talk about their relationships and how they feel about vampires.<br /> <br /> Our aim was to present these as playable characters, and so these are the character mindsets that we wrote in. I can understand the feeling that this departs from the norm, but part of the vampire's horror is how she ruins other people's lives by being too extra. So those people are bound to feel messy and complicated feelings about the vampire, and resentment is high up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and that's a major part of the tonal complaints.<br /> <br /> So far I've withheld feedback on the Ghouls section, but it feels more like 1e Ghouls because 1e Ghouls was written from their perspective too, and portraying power dynamics from the bottom up tends to lead our modern selves to view that as inherently abusive. I'd have preferred to see more nuanced takes that would help a player portray relationships that aid a healthy gaming table, for example: how do ghouls rationalize their relationship to a &quot;wrong&quot; creature? How do they rationalize the devil's bargain they took and can't get out of? How do they consider themselves and maintain their self-esteem and integrity (even, humanity). How do they husband and manage their little rebellions of attitude that tell them they're a person? Because--trust me on this one--even in a gaslit relationship of mingled genuine love and abuse, there's pure awareness of what's happening.<br /> <br /> Honestly, a person suffering from a &quot;[sense] of self-worth ... totally obliterated&quot; (p.94) and suffering from PTSD (which would be handy in context to detail the symptoms of, btw) as well as other mental issues--well that person is a particularly poor servant and really only useful as a display piece for the low cunning it takes to break a human. (This bit is from the Invictus &quot;bad guys&quot; section, but it stand out as a strong stroke of color both because it brings out the thread in other sections and conforms to &quot;expected norms&quot; of bad behavior by vamps.)<br /> <br /> Vampires invest their most precious resources into ghouls, and while some monsters would do so just to have a convenient dog to kick, you can get that without spending a willpower point to make an actual ghoul, and you can get someone slavishly devoted by chaining them up and spending three Vitae over three nights. Refresh yearly. A ghoul: made and maintained at least monthly with precious, precious vitae, is--and should be--reserved for something more, or it comes back to haunt the vamp in how their society views them. We rightfully judge our neighbors based on how they treat their animals, vamps would do the same.<br /> <br /> How do vampires interact with ghouls in such a way as to tend to their dog and avoid making it into a savage? Honestly, imagining abuse is pretty easy after VtM and VtR 1e books--focusing on something else is handy for players, storytellers and gaming tables. Focusing on, say, the <i>value</i> that ghouls represent, and how that helps drive the All-Night Society?<br /> <br /> Now, the Ghouls section delivers some of this. I'm re-skimming it while typing to minimize bias, and there are useful and thoughtful sections. The Covenant takes on ghouls is especially good (Invictus aside).<br /> <br /> Other than the disappointing tone, however, the ghoul section in particular falls flat for me once we reach the families part: some text is contradictory with preceding sections, and there is a broad lack of mechanics. Honestly? Ghoul families and unique ghoul twists are what the book has to offer in terms of new playable ideas. There is precious little to hang a character on, to instruct a Storyteller on what is expected. Family ghouls live longer (p. 104, sidebar), they get more &quot;touchstones&quot; (p. 105 sidebar, irrelevant as ghouls use Integrity), and a family benefit and drawback (p.105 same sidebar, &quot;Merits, bonuses to Skill Specialties, or access to a certain Discipline&quot; versus &quot;derangements or physical flaws&quot;). That's it. The example shows how &quot;Emma&quot; sets up the background for her ghoul family, and then there is nothing about on the selection of their characteristics--the most contentious part of a Storyteller's arbitration.<br /> <br /> Then we have 2.5 pages on the Crosses, and a sidebar giving an example of their merits and drawbacks. A <i>lot</i> of text, but the mechanics example is useful. Another 2.5 pages for the de Portocarreros; there is no mechanics sidebar at all. About 3 pages of text on the Golds; again, there is no mechanics block--wait, they do not suffer from addiction to Vitae? Or is it to the Vinculum? These are two different things! It sure would be nice to know how this works mechanically and they seem to have no drawback. Side note: 8-again on Occult for obscure sub-sects of a major religion != immunity to full Vinculum effects (I thought there was a merit that reduced Vinculum to a max of Stage 2, but cannot immediately find it). One of these things is not like the other--how do we benchmark a family mechanically then?<br /> <br /> So... we get maybe 1.5 examples of ghoul family mechanics. What about the rumor that in Japan are ghoul families who retain access to physical disciplines without Vitae? What about other mystical variations? Is there anything standard about a family, or just ST homebrew it? Oh what's this in Antagonists: &quot;Many Alley Men are familial ghouls, and therefore do not suffer the pull of hunger other ghouls possess&quot; (p. 121)--sounds awesome, are these Alley Men all Golds, then? Is this their benefit? Nothing is mentioned under systems.... is there something consistent that wasn't shared before?<br /> <br /> Ghoulish aberrations is better organized, with a clear &quot;systems&quot; tag and short text for each, and the mandragora creatures are bonus, but in several cases the flavor text is not satisfied by the systems provided. There is no provided example of &quot;ghouls who don't need regents&quot; as one example, and many more within the Gorged text. Conversely, the systems text for Phagians gives a useful mechanic for feeding from ghouls and when you get blood versus Vitae out of them--this SHOULD be lifted into earlier text as it's... kinda important in their interactions with vamps.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> This is not intended to be a full review of the section, but to illustrate the two main problems: tone and lack of mechanics. If you're not super-interested in using the <i>backstory</i> of the ghoul families, into mandragora, or like the couple special variations of ghouls, there's not much here you won't find in the main book or, especially, the 1e Ghouls book at much greater length. 2e uses its own mechanics and has its own themes--having that shine through would have helped.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:19:33-08:00","id":1165610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>impernious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165495#post1165495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you've hit a nail on a head here. This book is focused almost entirely on the experience of the half-damned characters. So their PoV colors how we talk about their relationships and how they feel about vampires.<br /> <br /> Our aim was to present these as playable characters, and so these are the character mindsets that we wrote in. I can understand the feeling that this departs from the norm, but part of the vampire's horror is how she ruins other people's lives by being too extra. So those people are bound to feel messy and complicated feelings about the vampire, and resentment is high up there.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, this is the same case as Beast, isn't? Some people didn't like that book either because It showed too much sympathy to a race of monsters who wreacked havoc and terror on the lives of people, sometimes breaking them into sociopathic Heroes (someone even called the book an exercise of gaslighting)...<br /> ...All without noticing the book was supposed to show the perspective of Beasts themselves. Everyone is the hero of his own narrative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:36:23-08:00","id":1165617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Khanwulf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165577#post1165577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (I thought there was a merit that reduced Vinculum to a max of Stage 2, but cannot immediately find it).<br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in the back of the core book with the other ghoul merits.<br /> Am I to assume that the new ghoul families don't have very clear rules or is it just this Gold family that has this problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 12-06-2017, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T10:41:46-08:00","id":1165620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165610#post1165610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is the same case as Beast, isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you apply an incredibly reductionist perspective to the issues people have had with each book, sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:04:02-08:00","id":1165627,"title":"","content":"Would a book written from the perspective of servants of vampires view vampires as inhuman abusive monsters?<br /> <br /> I mean... blood bond.<br /> <br /> Granted, I have no money and haven't read it, yet. I'd expect the Ghoul section at least to be downright worshipful, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T11:14:09-08:00","id":1165630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165617#post1165617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's in the back of the core book with the other ghoul merits.<br /> Am I to assume that the new ghoul families don't have very clear rules or is it just this Gold family that has this problem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Weakened Bond, three points; there it is. Thanks!<br /> <br /> Only the Crosses have an actual, honest (tiny) sidebar. The Golds have a (much bigger) sidebar with a bit of Kindred speculation about the Golds' reaction to vitae addicti-- no, Vinculum...? and the third family has nothing at all.<br /> <br /> The Alley Men are filed under Antagonists, which is a section with a consistent structure (&quot;systems&quot; ending paragraph). The Alley Men are presented both as a ghoul family, and as a classification of feral ghouls--it switches presentation from paragraph to paragraph in a most confusing manner. I pointed out another problem with them, above.<br /> <br /> @Maina: &quot;<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Would a book written from the perspective of servants of vampires view vampires as inhuman abusive monsters? </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I mean... blood bond.&quot;<br /> <br /> You [insert respectful gender pronoun of choice] win not one, not two, but <i>THREE</i> internets!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-15T20:02:31-08:00","id":1168104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1165610#post1165610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, this is the same case as Beast, isn't? .</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually the opposite. It seems a bit like 1E Requiem, where the game seemed a little <i>too </i>eager to emphasize, repeatedly, that vampires are not good people. It's tolerable, but annoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T10:26:05-08:00","id":1173255,"title":"","content":"Errata'd PDF is now up. <br /> <br /> Checked again on that one reference to &quot;werewolf Kinfolk&quot;...and apparently they opted to remove that line of text completely and replace it with a line about stigmatics from Demon. <br /> <br /> Well...that is technically a fix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T12:37:37-08:00","id":1173288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1173255#post1173255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Errata'd PDF is now up.<br /> <br /> Checked again on that one reference to &quot;werewolf Kinfolk&quot;...and apparently they opted to remove that line of text completely and replace it with a line about stigmatics from Demon.<br /> <br /> Well...that is technically a fix.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the same area vampires are no longer referred to as &quot;inherently evil&quot;. <br /> <br /> The two very important references to dhampir being immune to ghouling and the embrace are still quite scattered, however.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-04T22:13:11-08:00","id":1173411,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> &quot;spending three Vitae over three nights. Refresh yearly.&quot; where is this? I have not seen this previously though I may just be blind<br /> <br /> Edit: You were talking about blood bonds weren't you? I was thinking there was another way to get a year-long ghoul other than fealty's reward","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2909,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","user":"Mr.F.I.X.","date":". 01-05-2018, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-05T06:24:41-08:00","id":1173479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1123668-half-damned-what-do-we-know?p=1173411#post1173411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12493_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12493\" data-vbnamecard=\"12493\">Khanwulf</a> &quot;spending three Vitae over three nights. Refresh yearly.&quot; where is this? I have not seen this previously though I may just be blind<br /> <br /> Edit: You were talking about blood bonds weren't you? I was thinking there was another way to get a year-long ghoul other than fealty's reward</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope, sorry, just blood bonding.<br /> <br /> It would have been nice to have interesting merits in the book that tweaked the experiences of ghouls, making them less... reliable... in how the rules treated them. But alas that will remain in the realm of homebrew.<br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}